The conditions https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis are:
(a)the Owner-Driver is the registered Owner of the Vehicle insured;
(b)the Owner-Driver is the insured named in the policy;
(c)the Owner-Driver holds an effective Driving License, in accordance with the provisions of Law.
15(i).In The National Insurance Company Limited V. Poosamuthu and others,
[MANU/TN/3420/2022], cited supra, this Court also held that with reference to Section 163-A of the Motor Vehicles Act, 1988, the Hon'ble Supreme Court has taken a view that if a borrower of the vehicle met with an accident while riding the Vehicle, he cannot claim Compensation under Section 163-A of the Act.
